## 5. Distribution & Packaging Strategy

`loxia` uses `cargo-dist` alongside automated CI/CD pipelines to build, package, and release pre-compiled binaries and installers for all major operating systems upon every tag release.

```text
                                GitHub Release Matrix
                                          │
            ┌─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┐
            ▼                             ▼                             ▼
      Windows Target                macOS Target                  Linux Target
  ┌───────────────────┐         ┌───────────────────┐         ┌───────────────────┐
  │ • loxia-setup.msi │         │ • loxia-v0.1.0.dmg│         │ • loxia-bin (AUR) │
  │   (Bundles DLLs)  │         │ • Homebrew Tap    │         │ • loxia.tar.gz    │
  │ • loxia-win.zip   │         │ • loxia-mac.tar.gz│         │ • Homebrew Linux  │
  └───────────────────┘         └───────────────────┘         └───────────────────┘
```

### 5.1 Windows Packaging
* **Graphical Installer (`.msi`):** Built via WiX in `cargo-dist`. Embeds `mpv-1.dll` in `C:\Program Files\Loxia\` as a separate dynamic library so users do not need to manage C-libraries manually, and appends the directory to the system `PATH`.
* **Portable Archive (`.zip`):** Standalone zip file containing `loxia.exe` and `mpv-1.dll` for portable USB drives or non-admin systems.
* **Package Managers:** Scoop bucket manifest and WinGet submission.

### 5.2 macOS Packaging
* **Disk Image (`.dmg`) & Package (`.pkg`):** Drag-and-drop `.dmg` disk image containing `Loxia.app` launcher wrapper, and a standard `.pkg` installer placing the binary in `/usr/local/bin/loxia`.
* **Homebrew Tap:** Official custom tap repo (`brew tap your-username/tap && brew install loxia`).
* **Dependency Requirement:** Relies on system `mpv` via Homebrew (`brew install mpv`).

### 5.3 Linux Packaging
* **Arch User Repository (AUR):** `loxia-bin` PKGBUILD fetching pre-compiled GitHub release binaries.
* **Portable Tarball (`.tar.gz`):** Standalone static/dynamically linked binary distribution.
* **Homebrew for Linux:** Supported via the same Homebrew tap formula.

