## 10. Open Source Compliance, `libmpv` Bundling & Disclaimers

### 10.1 Legal Compliance & Dynamic Linking Guidelines
`loxia` links against `libmpv` using runtime dynamic linking. When bundling pre-built binaries (specifically `mpv-1.dll` on Windows), distribution MUST adhere to the terms of the **GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) v2.1 or later**:

1. **Dynamic Separation:** `mpv-1.dll` must remain a standalone dynamic library inside the installation directory (`C:\Program Files\Loxia\` or portable release zip). It must never be statically embedded or compiled directly into the `loxia.exe` binary, ensuring users can replace or upgrade the library file independently.
2. **License Distribution:** Every pre-compiled installer or distribution archive must include a copy of the LGPL license file (`LICENSE.LGPL` / `COPYING.LGPL`).
3. **Source Code Availability:** Documentation and release manifests must provide a clear pointer to the official upstream `mpv` source repository (https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv).

